Package: fixes
Type: Package
Title: Event Studies and Inference for Difference-in-Differences
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-10-21
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Yosuke", "Abe",
      email = "yosuke.abe0507@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Provides tools for event-study analysis and inference in
    difference-in-differences (DiD) designs with panel data, from the classic
    two-way fixed-effects (TWFE) event study to estimators for staggered
    adoption. Includes event_study() for event-study curves (dynamic effects
    by relative time), att() for aggregated ATT estimation (overall, by
    cohort, by calendar time), did() for basic two-way fixed-effects DiD, and
    honest_sensitivity() for sensitivity analysis under violations of
    parallel trends (Rambachan and Roth, 2023), all running on an internal
    C++ fixed-effects OLS engine. Supports multiple modern estimators:
    Callaway-Sant'Anna (2021), Sun-Abraham (2021), Borusyak-Jaravel-Spiess
    (2024), Wooldridge TWM, and Deb et al. FLEX. Results plot via base
    plot() methods.
